  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Why Does My Wall Tile Layout Look Off-Center?",
    "text": "Why Does My Wall Tile Layout Look Off-Center?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Ever wonder why a newly tiled wall can sometimes just feel... off? Often, it comes down to the initial layout. Many DIYers jump right in, starting from a corner or one side, and this can lead to awkward, narrow cuts at the edges that throw off the whole look. A pro, like HH Remodeling LLC, will typically start by finding the true center of the wall or establishing a strong reference line. This ensures a balanced design, even if the wall isn't perfectly square (which, let's be honest, most aren't!). You want to avoid those tiny, sliver-like pieces of tile that scream ",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
